\ Deadline: the plot. The day's timed events: the mail and the newspaper,
\ the telephone call Mrs. Robner wants to take in private, the reading of the
\ will, George's search of the hidden closet for the new will, and Sergeant
\ Duffy's trips to the laboratory. Accusing Ms. Dunbar once the evidence is
\ in sets off her meeting with Baxter in the shed, after which Baxter kills
\ her. An arrest ends the case with a letter from the commissioner.

\ the thing "it" refers to from now on
: this-is-it ( name -- )
	| name ^it-object ^it-location |
	name to it-object
	here to it-location ;

\ === the endings ===

\ the opening of the commissioner's letter that reports the verdict
: letter-heading ( date -- )
	| date |
	"Text of a letter from Police Commissioner Klutz dated " tell
	date tell
	":{nl}{nl}Dear Inspector,{nl}{nl}     " tell ;

' letter-heading embodies end-header

\ the investigation is over: begin it again, or stop
: offer-restart ( -- )
	end-line
	end-line
	"The case has ended.  Would you like to start your investigation over
	from scratch? (Y/N)" tell
	yes? if restart-game then
	quit-game ;

' offer-restart embodies case-over

: arrested-for-madness ( -- )
	"Your mind becomes confused amidst strange screaming, yelling, and the pangs
	of your conscience. ""How could I have done it?"" you ask yourself, as you
	hear the distant sound of police sirens. Sergeant Duffy and two other officers
	enter and grab you rather unceremoniously. They take you to a waiting car,
	where, forlorn and disgusted, you begin to ponder prison life. ""Perhaps,""
	you think, ""I shouldn't have done that.""" tell-line
	case-over ;

' arrested-for-madness embodies gone-crazy

\ the case solved: the author's summary, if wanted, and the end
: offer-summary ( -- )
	end-line
	"You have solved the case! If you would like, you may see the author's summary
	of the story. We would advise you to come up with your own first! Would you
	like to see the author's summary? (Y/N)" tell
	yes? if
		end-line
		"Mr. Robner's work was his life, as pointed out by a number of the principals.
		George knew that his father had lost control of the company, and a story in
		the newspaper indicated that Baxter intended to sell the company to a
		multi-national conglomerate, presumably to advance his career. Baxter admitted
		to the merger plans, but indicated that Mr. Robner was in complete agreement.
		This is contrary to what George and Mrs. Robner said. The note pad found in
		the library was Robner's last, desperate attempt to save the company, in which
		Robner threatened to expose Baxter's involvement in the Focus scandal. Baxter
		denied getting the note, but it was not in the trash. The papers detailing
		Baxter's criminality in the scandal were kept locked in a safe in a hidden
		closet near the library. Only George and Marshall Robner knew the whereabouts
		of the safe.{nl}  Baxter planned to murder his partner, aided by the fact that
		Robner was known to be depressed, even suicidal. He enlisted the help of his
		lover, Dunbar, one of whose medicines was found to interact fatally with the
		pills Robner was taking. The relationship of Baxter and Dunbar was kept quiet,
		although Mrs. Rourke had an inkling of it. After the concert in Hartford which
		both Baxter and Dunbar attended, they returned to the Robner estate. Dunbar
		placed some LoBlo in Robner's tea. After Robner died, Baxter used the ladder
		from the shed to enter the library and exchange the incriminating cup for a
		clean one (counting the china in the kitchen reveals that a cup is missing).
		Coming down the ladder, Baxter presumably dropped the cup and inadvertently
		left one piece on the ground in the rose garden, near the ladder holes that
		McNabb found while tending his roses.{nl}{nl}" tell
	then
	quit-game ;

\ Baxter and Dunbar arrested together: the verdict turns on the evidence found
: conspirators-arrested ( -- )
	:corpse-seen state if
		"Ms. Dunbar is dead!" tell-line
	else :dunbar-dead state if
		"Sergeant Duffy rushes into view. ""Ms. Dunbar is dead! She has
		shot herself in her room! Come quickly!"" He dashes off." tell-line
	else :baxter-papers :touched flag? :lab-report :touched flag? and :note-read state and :stub-d state and if
		end-line
		"September 5" end-header
		"Congratulations on your superb handling of the Robner case. As you have
		probably heard, a jury convicted Mr. Baxter and Ms. Dunbar today of the
		murder of Mr. Robner. Thanks to you, the murderers will be behind bars,
		possibly for the rest of their lives. Thanks for a job brilliantly done.
		Which reminds me of another fascinating case I would like to assign you
		to...{nl}{nl}Coming soon: Another INTERLOGIC Mystery from Infocom{nl}" tell-line
		offer-summary
	else present-time 700 < if
		"You realize the arrest would be a trifle premature, since you're not even
		sure that a murder was committed." tell-line
	else :lab-report :touched flag? not if
		end-line
		"August 19" end-header
		"The District Attorney has decided not to seek an indictment in the Robner
		case. He points out that it has never been proven that a murder was committed,
		despite the deep suspicions to the contrary. Thanks for your help on this
		case. It's too bad we couldn't find out more about the circumstances
		surrounding the death of Mr. Robner.{nl}{nl}" tell
	else :baxter-papers :touched flag? not if
		end-line
		"September 2" end-header
		"A grand jury looking into the death of Mr. Robner has decided not to indict
		the accused. They felt that the lack of motive as well as the contorted
		hypothesis involving the actual mechanism of the murder of Mr. Robner was not
		convincing. Personally, I think you're on the right track, but I must admit
		that the evidence is meager. Thank you for helping in the case.{nl}{nl}" tell
	else :note-read state not if
		end-line
		"October 4" end-header
		"The jury in the Robner case has declined to convict Mr. Baxter and Ms.
		Dunbar. Appearances indicate that the verdict was difficult, and that several
		jury members were convinced that the two were guilty. However, no evidence
		was presented directly relating the Focus case with the murder of Mr. Robner.
		This left the question of motive unresolved. I appreciate your efforts in the
		case and am sorry to report this outcome to you.{nl}{nl}" tell
	else
		end-line
		"October 6" end-header
		"The jury in the Robner case has declined to convict Mr. Baxter and Ms. Dunbar.
		Although most of the jury was convinced of their guilt, it seems that one or
		two felt there was some reasonable doubt about the proposed conspiracy. Their
		main concern was the lack of evidence that Baxter was near the grounds on the
		night of the murder. His alibi of having been to the symphony was confirmed by
		several people. Although this doesn't mean that he didn't go back to the
		Robner estate later, it nevertheless was not convincing. Thank you for your
		excellent efforts. It is sad to think that we may have let the murderers slip
		between our fingers.{nl}{nl}" tell
	then then then then then then then
	case-over ;

\ George and Baxter arrested together
: george-and-baxter-arrested ( -- )
	:lab-report :touched flag? not if
		"You realize that there is no evidence that a murder has been committed
		and decide not to go ahead with the arrest." tell-line
		exit
	then
	:new-will-seen state :george-run state 0 = not or
	:baxter-papers :touched flag? and :note-read state and if
		end-line
		"November 12" end-header
		" The district attorney, after extensive interrogation of George Robner and
		Mr. Baxter, has declined to seek an indictment against them. He agrees that
		there has been foul play in the death of Mr. Robner and that both suspects
		have motives for the crime. However, no coherent theory could be proposed
		which involved the two of them conspiring to murder Mr. Robner. On the other
		hand, it seems unlikely that either of them alone could have committed the
		crime. I am sorry that your work has gone for naught.{nl}{nl}" tell
	else
		end-line
		"August 1" end-header
		"The district attorney has declined to indict George Robner and Mr. Baxter
		in the death of Marshall Robner, noting that there is no link between the
		accused, except hatred, and that all of the evidence is circumstantial.
		I wish you luck on your future cases.{nl}{nl}" tell
	then
	case-over ;

\ an arrest of two people at once
: pair-arrested ( context -- result )
	drop
	[< :arrest >] verb? not if 0 exit then
	present-time 600 < if
		"It is rather early in the case to be making hasty judgments." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	:direct object-list to pair
	pair first to one
	pair second to other
	[< :baxter :global-baxter >] to baxter-names
	[< :dunbar :global-dunbar >] to dunbar-names
	[< :george :global-george >] to george-names
	baxter-names one has? dunbar-names other has? and
	dunbar-names one has? baxter-names other has? and or if
		conspirators-arrested
		1 exit
	then
	baxter-names one has? george-names other has? and
	george-names one has? baxter-names other has? and or if
		george-and-baxter-arrested
		1 exit
	then
	"You realize that this arrest is quite farfetched and would result
	only in your humiliation." tell-line
	1 ;

' pair-arrested :object-pair handles

\ === the mail and the newspaper ===

: mail-arrives ( context -- result )
	drop
	here :front-path = here :foyer = :front-door :open flag? and or if
		"A mailman walks briskly up to you, hands you an envelope,
		and departs." tell-line
		:envelope winner move-to
		:envelope :touched set-flag
		1 exit
	then
	here :foyer = if
		"There is a short rap on the front door.  A moment later, a thin
		envelope appears under the door." tell-line
		:envelope :foyer move-to
		"Partially exposed under the front door is an envelope." :envelope :initial-description property!
		:i-mail-2 60 queue enable
		1 exit
	then
	:envelope :foyer-table move-to
	:i-mail-2 60 queue enable
	[ :south-lawn :west-of-door :east-of-door ] here position-of 0 >= if
		"You notice a mailman stop by the house briefly and depart." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	0 ;

' mail-arrives :i-mail handles

\ an hour later Mrs. Rourke goes for the mail left in the foyer
: mail-waiting ( context -- result )
	drop
	[ :foyer :foyer-table ] :envelope location-of position-of 0 >= if
		:rourke :foyer true establish-goal
		:i-mail-3 -1 queue enable
	then
	0 ;

' mail-waiting :i-mail-2 handles

\ Mrs. Rourke takes the mail to Mrs. Robner
: mail-delivered ( context -- result )
	drop
	:rourke-mail state if
		:rourke :mrs-robner location-of inside? not if 0 exit then
		:i-mail-3 0 queue drop
		:rourke :rourke-room true establish-goal
		:envelope winner inside? winner :mrs-robner location-of inside? and if
			"Mrs. Rourke walks up to Mrs. Robner. ""I'm sorry, Ma'am, but this gentleman
			has a letter that just arrived for you."" Mrs. Robner grabs the letter from
			you. ""That is none of your business!""" tell-line
		else :envelope :rourke inside? not if
			1 exit
		then then
		here :rourke location-of = not if
			:envelope remove-thing
			0 exit
		then
		:envelope :rourke inside? if
			"Mrs. Rourke hands an envelope to Mrs. Robner." tell
		then
		:envelope :mrs-robner move-to
		:envelope-opened state if
			" Mrs. Robner examines the
			envelope, then turns to you. ""You did this, I suppose."" she says. ""You had
			no right! I expected better treatment than this. You would think I were
			suspected of wrongdoing!""" tell-line
		else
			" Mrs. Robner examines
			the envelope briefly, then puts it in her pocket." tell-line
			:envelope remove-thing
		then
		1 exit
	then
	:rourke :foyer inside? not if 0 exit then
	[ :foyer-table :foyer ] :envelope location-of position-of 0 < if
		:rourke unprioritize
		0 exit
	then
	:envelope :rourke move-to
	:envelope :touched set-flag
	:rourke :mrs-robner location-of true establish-goal
	true :rourke-mail state!
	here :foyer = if
		"Mrs. Rourke takes the envelope and starts to walk away." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	0 ;

' mail-delivered :i-mail-3 handles

: newspaper-arrives ( context -- result )
	drop
	:newspaper :front-path move-to
	[ :south-lawn :front-path ] here position-of 0 >= if
		"The local paperboy, in an amazing athletic feat, throws a newspaper toward
		the house from a distance of at least 100 feet. It even lands beside the front
		door, rather than in the bushes." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	0 ;

' newspaper-arrives :i-newspaper handles

\ === the reading of the will ===

\ George's calendar question sends him to his room to wait for a chance at the library
: george-hurries ( -- )
	:george location-of to place
	place here = if
		place :george-room = if
			"George paces around. ""I just remembered,"" he says, ""I've got some personal
			business to attend to. Would you mind?"" He shows you to the door." tell-line
		else place :line property upstairs-line = if
			"""I'm...I really have some business to do in my room. I'll speak
			to you later,"" George says. He starts off toward his room." tell-line
		else
			"""I've...got to be going now. I'll see you later,"" George says.
			He starts to leave." tell-line
		then then
	then
	place :george-room = not if :george :george-room true establish-goal then
	true :george-sequence state!
	:i-george-hack -1 queue enable ;

' george-hurries embodies george-hack

: george-hurries-later ( context -- result )
	drop
	george-hurries
	1 ;

' george-hurries-later :george-hack handles

\ the will read or given up: Coates leaves
: will-concluded ( -- )
	:coates :south-lawn true establish-goal
	present-time :will-time state!
	true :post-will state!
	:i-will-reading 0 queue drop
	:g-calendar state if george-hack then ;

: will-reading ( context -- result )
	drop
	[ :mrs-robner :dunbar :baxter :george ] ( person | person :living-room inside? not ) find-first null? not to someone-missing
	present-time 760 < someone-missing and if
		true :will-hold state!
		:i-will-reading -1 queue drop
		here :living-room = not if 0 exit then
		70 probability if 0 exit then
		50 probability if
			"Mr. Coates asks everyone to be patient, as not everyone is present." tell-line
		else
			"Mr. Coates appears distracted, looking frequently toward the door." tell-line
		then
		1 exit
	then
	here :living-room = not if
		:will-wait state 1+ dup :will-wait state! 15 > if
			:i-will-missed -1 queue enable
			will-concluded
			0 exit
		then
		:i-will-reading -1 queue drop
		0 exit
	then
	true :at-reading state!
	present-time 720 > :will-wait state 3 > and if
		"The people present turn to look at you. Mrs. Robner glares at you. ""You
		might at least have the courtesy to be here on time! Haven't you caused enough
		disruption already? We should have started without you. Mr. Coates, please
		proceed.""" tell-line
	else present-time 760 > if
		"""It's late, so let's begin!"" Coates says." tell-line
	else :will-hold state if
		"""Ah!"" Mr. Coates says, ""Everybody's here now.""" tell-line
	then then then
	"Mr. Coates begins: ""This is an awkward situation. Mr. Robner told me five
	days ago that he wanted to execute a new will, and promised to call me when
	it was completed. As I never heard from him, I must assume that he either
	changed his mind or did not complete the new will. Therefore, the one in my
	possession must be considered the most recent testament.""" tell-line
	:g-calendar state if
		"You notice that George, who was not initially paying close attention, now
		perks up and begins to look about anxiously." tell-line
	else
		"From the corner of your eye, you catch George nodding his head, as
		if in approval, and smiling broadly." tell-line
	then
	"Continuing, Mr. Coates says: ""Naturally, should a more recent will exist
	and be found within a reasonable period, the present one will be voided.
	I will proceed with reading the will here in my hands, which was executed
	three years ago last month."" He reads the will, simply written and direct,
	leaving equal parts of the estate to his son, George Arthur Robner, and
	his wife, Mrs. Leslie Phillips Robner." tell-line
	"There is some discussion, understated congratulations and overstated
	sympathy, which Mr. Coates cuts short by clearing his throat. ""I must
	leave now, I'm afraid. If you have any questions, I can be contacted
	tomorrow."" He picks up the phone, dials his office, and asks to be
	picked up at the Robner estate." tell-line
	:g-calendar state if
		"George, now looking quite upset, starts for the door." tell-line
	then
	will-concluded
	1 ;

' will-reading :i-will-reading handles

\ Mrs. Robner or Mr. Coates remarks on the inspector's absence from the reading
: will-missed ( context -- result )
	drop
	:mrs-robner here inside? if
		"Mrs. Robner turns to you. ""I don't understand why you missed the will
		reading. You seem so interested in everything else that goes on around
		here.""" tell-line
		:i-will-missed 0 queue drop
		1 exit
	then
	:coates here inside? if
		"Mr. Coates says, in passing, ""To tell you the truth, Inspector, my
		suspicions about this case are not quite allayed. I wish you had been
		at the will reading. Good day.""" tell-line
		:i-will-missed 0 queue drop
		1 exit
	then
	0 ;

' will-missed :i-will-missed handles

\ === George and the new will ===

\ George in his room, waiting to be alone; every minute until he gets into the library
: george-waits-alone ( context -- result )
	drop
	:george location-of to place
	:george goal-of to goal
	:george-ready state if
		here place = if
			false :george-ready state!
			false :george-scream state!
			1 :george-wait state!
			"""I don't understand you, Inspector. I asked to be alone so I can take care
			of some business. I...I don't see why you have to snoop around here like I was
			some sort of suspect.""" tell-line
			:george-scream state if
				"""I said to close that door and not to come in! You must be deaf as well as
				stupid!""" tell-line
			then
			1 exit
		then
		:george-door :open flag? :george-scream state not and if
			"As the door opens, you hear George say ""Close that door! I'm working!""" tell-line
			true :george-scream state!
			1 exit
		then
		0 exit
	then
	:george-wait state if
		here place = if
			"George paces around the room, awaiting your departure with ill-concealed
			impatience." tell-line
			:george-wait state 1+ dup :george-wait state! 12 > if
				"""I can't take this. You get on my nerves. I'm leaving.""" tell-line
				here goal@queued = if :living-room goal!queued then
				:george unprioritize
				false :george-wait state!
				:i-george-hack 0 queue drop
				:george-hack 30 queue enable
			then
			1 exit
		then
		false :george-wait state!
		:george-door :open clear-flag
		[ :library :corridor-4 :corridor-3 ] here position-of 0 >= if
			"You hear George's door close." tell-line
			1 exit
		then
		0 exit
	then
	place :george-room = if
		here place = if
			"""I have business to attend to. Would you mind leaving?""" tell-line
			1 :george-wait state!
			1 exit
		then
		:i-george-hack-2 5 queue enable
		true :george-ready state!
		false to door-heard
		[ :corridor-4 :corridor-3 ] here position-of 0 >= :george-door :open flag? and if
			:george-door :open clear-flag
			true to door-heard
			"You hear George's door close." tell-line
		then
		:george-door :open clear-flag
		door-heard if 1 else 0 then exit
	then
	here place = if
		:george-follow state not if
			true :george-follow state!
			0 exit
		then
		50 probability if
			"""Please stop following me around like this. Can I have no privacy? I'm
			simply trying to take care of something personal.""" tell-line
		else
			"""Stop following me. My business is private.""" tell-line
		then
		1 exit
	then
	place :corridor-4 = if
		here corridor-bits 1 bit-and 1 = if
			"George glances in your direction, then enters his room." tell-line
			:george :george-room move-to
			1 exit
		then
		0 exit
	then
	[ :corridor-3 :corridor-2 ] place position-of 0 >= [ :corridor-1 :stair-top ] here position-of 0 >= and if
		"George glances back at you briefly, then continues on his way." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	0 ;

' george-waits-alone :i-george-hack handles

\ George looks out for a clear hallway, and crosses to the library when there is one
: george-peeks-out ( context -- result )
	drop
	:george-ready state not if
		:i-george-hack-2 9 random-below 1+ queue drop
		0 exit
	then
	here corridor-bits 1 bit-and 1 = here :library = or if
		:i-george-hack-2 9 random-below 1+ queue drop
		[ :corridor-2 :corridor-1 :stair-top ] here position-of 0 >= if
			30 probability if
				"A door opens down the hall. George steps out, spots you, and looks briefly
				toward the window. After a moment he steps back into his room and shuts the
				door." tell-line
			else
				"You faintly hear a door open and then close near the end of the hall." tell-line
			then
			1 exit
		then
		[ :corridor-4 :library ] here position-of 0 >= if
			"You hear George's door open and " tell
			30 probability if
				"you catch a brief glimpse of his
				head darting back into the doorway. You watch as the door closes again." tell-line
			else
				"close again immediately." tell-line
			then
			1 exit
		then
		:george-door :open flag? if
			:george-door :open clear-flag
			"George walks up to his door and slams it in your face." tell-line
			1 exit
		then
		here :corridor-3 = if
			"George opens his door and peeks out. He is startled by your presence,
			excuses himself, and closes the door sharply in your face before you can
			utter a word." tell-line
			1 exit
		then
		0 exit
	then
	:i-george-hack 0 queue drop
	:george :library move-to
	:george-door :open set-flag
	:i-george-hack-2 0 queue drop
	:i-george-hack-3 -1 queue enable
	here :upstairs-closet = if
		"You hear George's door open and you see his head poke out briefly, scanning
		the hallway. He apparently didn't see you, and darts across the hall to the
		library." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	here :library-balcony = if
		"You see George through the doorway, looking down the hallway, then darting
		into the library." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	0 ;

' george-peeks-out :i-george-hack-2 handles

\ George in the hidden closet, minute by minute: in, the shelf closed, the safe opened, out with the new will
: george-searches ( context -- result )
	drop
	false to seen
	:george-search state to minute
	minute 0 = if
		here :library-balcony = if
			"George walks purposefully toward the bookshelves. He looks around, but you
			react before he can see you. When you peek out again, George is fiddling with
			the shelves. His right arm reaches into the shelf and, to your amazement, the
			unit of bookshelves on the left rotates away from the wall, revealing a
			darkened room behind. George enters it, trembling with barely controlled fear
			and excitement." tell-line
			true to seen
			true :books-moved state!
			true :george-moves-books state!
			:george :hidden-closet move-to
		else here :library = if
			"George hears you walk through the balcony doors and recoils in horror. He
			runs across the hall to his own bedroom, slamming his door shut." tell-line
			true to seen
			false :george-ready state!
			false :george-wait state!
			:george-door :open clear-flag
			:george :george-room move-to
			:i-george-hack-3 0 queue drop
			:i-george-hack-2 10 queue drop
		else
			:george :hidden-closet move-to
			true :books-moved state!
		then then
	else minute 1 = if
		[ :library :library-balcony ] here position-of 0 >= if
			"A dim light in the hidden closet comes on. In the faint light, you can see
			George motioning with his right hand. All at once, the shelf swings shut!" tell-line
			true to seen
		then
	else minute 10 < if
		:hidden-door-l :open flag? if
			"As the bookshelf swings open, you see George carefully dialing a combination
			into a large wall safe. He turns in panic and, with an exclamation, knocks you
			down and bolts out of the library." tell-line
			true to seen
			true :safe-seen state!
			0 :george-search state!
			:i-george-hack-3 0 queue drop
			:george :corridor-1 move-to
			:george :east-lawn true establish-goal
		then
	else minute 16 < if
		:hidden-door-l :open flag? if
			:safe :open set-flag
			true :safe-seen state!
			"As the shelf swings open, George spins to face you. His expression, first
			seemingly wild with happiness, changes to one of panic and horror. He jerks
			around, trying feebly to conceal a piece of paper in his hands. He jumps
			toward you, then recoils in fear. Finally, sobbing, he crumples to the floor,
			clutching the paper beneath him. A large combination safe, imbedded in a wall,
			is lying open. You enter the hidden closet." tell-line
			true to seen
			:i-george-hack-3 0 queue drop
			:new-will :george move-to
			:hidden-closet true goto
			:i-george-leave-closet 10 queue enable
			true :new-will-seen state!
		then
	else minute 16 = if
		:safe :open clear-flag
		here :library = if
			"Suddenly, the bookshelves swing out, forming an opening to a dark area
			behind. George starts to emerge but stops suddenly as he notices you! With
			jack-rabbit reflexes, he darts back inside.  Before you can act, the
			shelves close again." tell-line
			true to seen
			:george :north-lawn move-to
			:soggy-will :lake move-to
			:new-will remove-thing
			:i-george-hack-3 0 queue drop
			present-time :george-run state!
		else
			:george :library move-to
			:i-george-hack-3 0 queue drop
			:george unprioritize
			:george :north-lawn true establish-goal
			here :library-balcony = if
				"Suddenly, the shelf swings out, and George emerges. He walks over to a
				special place in the shelves and reaches behind some books. The bookshelves
				silently assume their normal position." tell-line
				true to seen
			then
		then
	then then then then then
	:george-search state 1+ :george-search state!
	seen if 1 else 0 then ;

' george-searches :i-george-hack-3 handles

: george-leaves-closet ( context -- result )
	drop
	:george :hidden-closet inside? if :george :george-room false establish-goal then
	0 ;

' george-leaves-closet :i-george-leave-closet handles

\ === the telephone call ===

\ Mrs. Robner goes up to take the call in her bedroom
: call-from-bedroom ( -- )
	:mrs-robner location-of :robner-old-location state!
	:mrs-robner :master-bedroom true establish-goal
	true :call-move state!
	:i-call -1 queue drop ;

\ Mrs. Robner shuts herself in with the phone
: call-in-private ( -- )
	false :call-move state!
	1 :call-in-progress state!
	:master-bedroom-door :open clear-flag
	here :corridor-1 = if
		"Mrs. Robner shuts the door to the master bedroom." tell-line
	else [ :corridor-2 :stair-top ] here position-of 0 >= if
		"You hear the master bedroom door shut." tell-line
	then then ;

\ the phone rings for Mrs. Robner, who calls back from her bedroom when she can be alone
: telephone-rings ( context -- result )
	drop
	:mrs-robner location-of to robner-place
	:call-ring state if
		robner-place :living-room = if
			false :call-ring state!
			here :living-room = if
				"Mrs. Robner picks up the phone. ""Oh, hi. Look, I can't talk now. I'll call
				you later, okay? Bye, then."" She hangs up the phone." tell-line
				call-from-bedroom
				1 exit
			then
			call-from-bedroom
			0 exit
		then
		"The phone rings again." tell-line
		:telephone here global-in? if :telephone this-is-it then
		1 exit
	then
	:call-in-progress state if
		:call-in-progress state 1+ dup :call-in-progress state! 15 > if
			false :call-in-progress state!
			:i-call 0 queue drop
			:mrs-robner unprioritize
			0 exit
		then
		:master-bedroom-door :open flag? here :master-bedroom = or if
			"Mrs. Robner speaks quietly into the phone and hangs up." tell-line
			false :call-in-progress state!
			:i-call 0 queue drop
			:mrs-robner unprioritize
			1 exit
		then
		0 exit
	then
	:call-waiting state if
		[ robner-place :master-bath :bedroom-balcony ] here position-of 0 < if
			call-in-private
			0 exit
		then
		:call-waiting state 1+ dup :call-waiting state! 3 > not if
			"Mrs. Robner glares at you, holding the phone in one hand. ""Would you
			mind terribly?"", she asks." tell-line
			1 exit
		then
		:call-move state if
			"""I can't understand why you won't let me use the phone. Can't I talk to
			my best friend? Hummph...I suppose it can wait, since you are being
			so...uh...unhelpful."" She puts down the receiver, rises from her bed, and
			starts to leave." tell-line
			false :call-move state!
			false :call-waiting state!
		else
			"""I give up. What IS your problem, anyway?,"" Mrs. Robner asks, in a
			barely controllable rage. ""I'll call you back,"" she says, and slams down
			the receiver." tell-line
			false :call-move state!
		then
		:i-call 0 queue drop
		:mrs-robner unprioritize
		1 exit
	then
	:call-move state if
		robner-place :master-bedroom = not if 0 exit then
		[ :bedroom-balcony :master-bath :master-bedroom ] here position-of 0 < if
			call-in-private
			0 exit
		then
		here :master-bedroom = not if
			"Mrs. Robner enters her bedroom and spots you." tell-line
		then
		"""I'd like to make a private phone call, if you have no objection,"" she
		says. She motions toward the door." tell-line
		1 :call-waiting state!
		1 exit
	then
	[ :library :living-room :master-bedroom ] here position-of 0 >= if
		"The telephone rings." tell-line
		:telephone this-is-it
		:mrs-robner :living-room true establish-goal
		true :call-ring state!
		:i-call -1 queue drop
		1 exit
	then
	here robner-place = if
		"You can hear a telephone ringing in a nearby room. Mrs. Robner
		says ""Pardon me"" and starts for the door." tell-line
		true :call-ring state!
		:i-call -1 queue drop
		:mrs-robner :living-room true establish-goal
		1 exit
	then
	here :line property outside-line = not if
		"You hear a phone ringing in a nearby room." tell-line
		true :call-ring state!
		:i-call -1 queue drop
		:mrs-robner :living-room true establish-goal
		1 exit
	then
	50 probability if
		"You notice a very faint ringing sound coming from the house." tell-line
		call-from-bedroom
		1 exit
	then
	0 ;

' telephone-rings :i-call handles

\ === Sergeant Duffy and the laboratory ===

\ Duffy takes the direct object to the laboratory, for fingerprints or, with analysis?, for a chemical analysis against the indirect object if one is named
: send-to-laboratory ( analysis? -- result )
	| analysis? |
	:fingerprint-object state if
		"Sergeant Duffy is already at the lab running a previous errand.
		You will have to wait for him to return." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	analysis? not if
		"You look at the " tell object tell-name " closely. It appears to have good
		fingerprints on it, so you call for Sergeant Duffy." tell-line
	then
	analysis? indirect null? not and if indirect else false then :analysis-goal state!
	object :fingerprint-object state!
	analysis? :analysis-object state!
	object :ladder = if
		present-time 720 > if
			"Sergeant Duffy arrives and shakes his head sadly. ""I'm sorry, sir, but
			the Ladder Analysis Department closes at noon."" He leaves." tell-line
			false :fingerprint-object state!
			0 exit
		then
		false :ladder-flag state!
		false :ladder-flag-2 state!
		:ladder :undescribed clear-flag
	then
	:i-fingerprint 15 random-below 1+ 15 + queue enable
	object remove-thing
	object :touched set-flag
	"Sergeant Duffy walks up as quietly as a mouse. He takes the " tell object tell-name " from
	you. ""I'll return soon with the results,"" he says, and leaves as silently as
	he entered." tell-line
	1 ;

( true send-to-laboratory ) embodies analyze-in-laboratory

\ Duffy returns with the results and the evidence
: laboratory-results ( context -- result )
	drop
	:fingerprint-object state to evidence
	"Sergeant Duffy " tell
	evidence :ladder = if
		"comes onto the scene. " tell
	else 30 probability if
		"appears before you, holding the " tell evidence tell-name
		" carefully in his hands. His quiet efficiency and youthful vigor impress you
		quite a bit. " tell
	else 50 probability if
		"seems to arrive from nowhere, holding the " tell evidence tell-name
		" in his hands. " tell
	else
		"returns with the " tell evidence tell-name ".  For a moment you muse on his almost
		magical entrances. " tell
	then then then
	:analysis-goal state to compared-with
	:analysis-object state not if
		"""The fingerprints,"" he begins,
		""belong to " tell
		evidence :cup = if
			"Mr. Robner" tell
		else [ :saucer :sugar-bowl ] evidence position-of 0 >= if
			"Mr. Robner and Ms. Dunbar" tell
		then then
	else compared-with if
		evidence :fragment = [ :loblo :loblo-bottle :global-loblo ] compared-with position-of 0 >= and if
			"""The fragment did contain LoBlo. Here is the full report.""
			He hands you a slip of paper, and departs." tell-line
			:lab-report :player move-to
			:lab-report :touched set-flag
			evidence :player move-to
			false :fingerprint-object state!
			1 exit
		then
		"""The " tell evidence tell-name " analysis yielded nothing useful" tell
	else evidence :fragment = if
		"""The fragment,"" he begins,
		""contains traces of tea and sugar." tell
		" In addition, there seems to be some other chemical
		present that is not a common medication. It could take weeks to determine
		exactly what it is. It is definitely not Amitraxin (Ebullion), though. There
		are no clear fingerprints" tell
	else evidence :cup = if
		"""The cup,"" he begins,
		""contains a trace of tea. The fingerprints are those of Mr. Robner" tell
	else evidence :saucer = if
		"""The saucer,"" he begins,
		""contains traces of tea and sugar. The fingerprints are
		those of Mr. Robner and Ms. Dunbar" tell
	else evidence :sugar-bowl = if
		"""The bowl,"" he begins,
		""has the fingerprints of Mr. Robner and Ms. Dunbar. The bowl
		contains common table sugar only." tell
	else
		"""I am sorry,"" he begins,
		"" but the lab found nothing of interest." tell
	then then then then then then
	evidence :ladder = here :line property outside-line = not and if
		" In the interests of
		civility, I have left the ladder outside the house."" He leaves." tell-line
		:ladder :front-path move-to
	else
		""".
		With that, he leaves, handing you the " tell evidence tell-name
		" as he whisks away." tell-line
		evidence :player move-to
	then
	false :fingerprint-object state!
	1 ;

' laboratory-results :i-fingerprint handles

\ === Ms. Dunbar's meeting with Baxter ===

\ accused, Ms. Dunbar goes to find Baxter
: dunbar-seeks-baxter ( -- )
	:baxter location-of to baxter-place
	:dunbar-accused state if exit then
	:dunbar baxter-place inside? not if :dunbar baxter-place true establish-goal then
	true :dunbar-accused state!
	baxter-place :dunbar-sequence-baxter-location state!
	:i-dunbar-seq -1 queue enable ;

' dunbar-seeks-baxter embodies dunbar-sequence

\ whether a person is here or in sight along a corridor
: followed? ( person -- flag )
	| person |
	person location-of to place
	place here = if true exit then
	here :guest-room = if false exit then
	place corridor-bits here corridor-bits bit-and 0 = not ;

\ Ms. Dunbar reaches Baxter and has a word with him out of the inspector's hearing
: dunbar-finds-baxter ( context -- result )
	drop
	:baxter location-of to baxter-place
	:baxter goal-of to baxter-goal
	baxter-place :dunbar-sequence-baxter-location state = not if
		dunbar-sequence
		0 exit
	then
	:dunbar location-of baxter-place = not if 0 exit then
	false baxter-goal!enabled
	here baxter-place = if
		"Ms. Dunbar glances at Baxter and then at you." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	true :dunbar-baxter-meet state!
	true baxter-goal!enabled
	:i-dunbar-seq 0 queue drop
	:i-dunbar-seq-2 5 queue enable
	0 ;

' dunbar-finds-baxter :i-dunbar-seq handles

: dunbar-heads-for-shed ( context -- result )
	drop
	false :dunbar-baxter-meet state!
	:dunbar :shed-room true establish-goal
	:i-dunbar-seq-d -1 queue enable
	:i-dunbar-seq-3 10 queue enable
	0 ;

' dunbar-heads-for-shed :i-dunbar-seq-2 handles

: baxter-heads-for-lawn ( context -- result )
	drop
	:baxter :north-lawn true establish-goal
	:i-dunbar-seq-b -1 queue enable
	0 ;

' baxter-heads-for-lawn :i-dunbar-seq-3 handles

\ Ms. Dunbar on her way to the shed, wary of being followed, and waiting there for Baxter
: dunbar-walks-to-shed ( context -- result )
	drop
	:dunbar goal-of to dunbar-goal
	:dunbar :shed-room inside? if
		:baxter :shed-room inside? if
			:i-dunbar-seq-4 -1 queue enable
			:i-dunbar-seq-d 0 queue drop
			0 exit
		then
		here :shed-room = if
			50 probability if
				"Dunbar paces around the shed nervously. If she was looking for something,
				she would have found it by now." tell-line
			else
				"Ms. Dunbar seems to be looking around for something." tell-line
			then
			1 exit
		then
		0 exit
	then
	here :line property outside-line = :dunbar followed? and not if
		true dunbar-goal!enabled
		0 exit
	then
	dunbar-goal@enabled if
		false dunbar-goal!enabled
	else 28 probability if
		"Ms. Dunbar eyes you nervously." tell-line
		1 exit
	else 50 probability if
		"Ms. Dunbar stares off toward the south." tell-line
		1 exit
	else
		"Ms. Dunbar seems to be deep in thought." tell-line
		1 exit
	then then then
	:stub-dropped state not here :line property outside-line = and if
		"Ms. Dunbar spots you and stops. She reaches into her pocket and pulls out a
		cigarette. As she does so, what appears to be a ticket stub falls out of her
		pocket and floats to the ground. She checks her pocket again, apparently for
		a match, but finds none and puts the cigarette back in her pocket." tell-line
		:stub :dunbar location-of move-to
		true :stub-dropped state!
		1 exit
	then
	15 probability if
		"Ms. Dunbar glances around as she walks. She takes a quick glance in your
		direction, but it doesn't seem like she noticed you." tell-line
		true dunbar-goal!enabled
		1 exit
	then
	50 probability if
		"Ms. Dunbar looks around as she walks and does a brief double-take
		when she looks in your direction. She slows down and stops." tell-line
		1 exit
	then
	"Ms. Dunbar, who has been looking from side to side as she goes,
	comes to a stop. She spins around, looking in all directions." tell-line
	1 ;

' dunbar-walks-to-shed :i-dunbar-seq-d handles

: baxter-heads-for-shed ( context -- result )
	drop
	:baxter :north-lawn inside? here :line property upstairs-line = or if
		:i-dunbar-seq-b 0 queue drop
		:baxter :shed-room true establish-goal
		:i-dunbar-seq-b-2 -1 queue enable
	then
	0 ;

' baxter-heads-for-shed :i-dunbar-seq-b handles

\ Baxter on his way to the shed, pausing when he is followed
: baxter-walks-to-shed ( context -- result )
	drop
	:baxter goal-of to baxter-goal
	:baxter :shed-room inside? if
		:i-dunbar-seq-b-2 0 queue drop
		0 exit
	then
	:baxter followed? not if
		true baxter-goal!enabled
		0 exit
	then
	baxter-goal@enabled if
		false baxter-goal!enabled
		0 exit
	then
	50 probability if
		"Baxter draws a deep breath and looks about contentedly." tell-line
	else
		"Baxter stares out over the lake." tell-line
	then
	1 ;

' baxter-walks-to-shed :i-dunbar-seq-b-2 handles

\ the meeting over, Ms. Dunbar goes to her room and Baxter to the north lawn
: meeting-ends ( -- )
	[ :east-lawn :east-side :east-of-door ] here position-of 0 >= if
		"Baxter and Dunbar both leave the shed, heading off in
		different directions." tell-line
	else here :behind-shed = if
		"The voices stop and you hear sets of footsteps leaving the shed." tell-line
	then then
	:dunbar :dunbar-room true establish-goal
	:baxter :north-lawn true establish-goal
	:i-baxter-seq -1 queue enable
	:i-dunbar-seq-4 0 queue drop
	:secret-meeting state :meeting-interrupted state!
	0 :secret-meeting state! ;

\ Ms. Dunbar and Baxter argue in the shed until the inspector walks in or the argument ends
: shed-meeting ( context -- result )
	drop
	here :shed-room = if
		:secret-meeting state to meeting
		meeting 2 < meeting 5 > or if
			"You seem to have walked in on some sort of get-together, although from the
			look on Ms. Dunbar's face, you are not the guest of honor. She is aghast, and
			she continually looks back and forth between Mr. Baxter and yourself." tell-line
		else
			"As you enter the shed, Mr. Baxter and Ms. Dunbar, who were in the midst of a
			quiet but heated argument, stop at once. Ms. Dunbar is quite upset and
			clutches Mr. Baxter. Baxter, who has retained his composure throughout,
			attempts to comfort Dunbar. She pushes him away and runs out of the shed." tell-line
			:dunbar :east-lawn move-to
			:dunbar :character property to dunbar-number
			last-seen dunbar-number @i present-time 0 !i drop
			last-seen 0 @i present-time dunbar-number !i drop
		then
		meeting-ends
		1 exit
	then
	:baxter :shed-room inside? if
		:secret-meeting state 1+ dup :secret-meeting state! 5 > if meeting-ends then
	then
	0 ;

' shed-meeting :i-dunbar-seq-4 handles

\ === Baxter kills Ms. Dunbar ===

\ the household runs to Ms. Dunbar's room
: shot-heard ( -- )
	:mrs-robner :dunbar-room true establish-goal
	:rourke :corridor-1 true establish-goal
	:george :dunbar-room true establish-goal
	:i-shot -1 queue enable ;

\ Baxter climbs the ladder to the bedroom balcony, crosses to Ms. Dunbar's room unseen, and shoots her
: baxter-strikes ( context -- result )
	drop
	:baxter-seq-loc state to stage
	stage :master-bedroom = if
		here corridor-bits 1 bit-and 1 = not
		[ :stairs :stair-bottom :dunbar-room ] here position-of 0 < and if
			:bedroom-balcony :baxter-seq-loc state!
			:baxter :bedroom-balcony move-to
			:dunbar remove-thing
			true :dunbar-dead state!
			:i-dunbar interrupt disable
			:pistol :dunbar-room move-to
			:suicide-note :dunbar-room move-to
			:corpse :dunbar-room move-to
			:i-baxter-seq 0 queue drop
			:i-baxter-escape -1 queue enable
			here :line property upstairs-line = if
				true :shot-fired state!
				"You hear a pistol shot close by." tell-line
			else here :line property outside-line = if
				"You hear what sounds like a pistol shot from inside the house." tell-line
			else
				"From upstairs, you hear a single explosion like a pistol shot." tell-line
			then then
			shot-heard
			1 exit
		then
		0 exit
	then
	stage :bedroom-balcony = if
		here :master-bedroom = not :mrs-robner location-of :master-bedroom = not and if
			:baxter :master-bedroom move-to
			:master-bedroom :baxter-seq-loc state!
		then
		0 exit
	then
	stage :north-lawn = if
		:dunbar :dunbar-room inside? here :line property outside-line = not and here :bedroom-balcony = not and if
			true :ladder-flag-2 state!
			false :ladder-flag state!
			:ladder :orchard move-to
			:ladder :undescribed clear-flag
			:ladder :touched set-flag
			:baxter :bedroom-balcony move-to
			:bedroom-balcony :baxter-seq-loc state!
		then
		0 exit
	then
	:baxter :north-lawn inside? if :north-lawn :baxter-seq-loc state! then
	0 ;

' baxter-strikes :i-baxter-seq handles

\ Baxter runs back to the balcony and down the ladder, glimpsed if the inspector is near
: baxter-escapes ( context -- result )
	drop
	false to seen
	:shot-fired state if
		false :shot-fired state!
		[ :corridor-4 :corridor-3 ] here position-of 0 >= if
			"As you enter the hallway, you catch a glimpse of someone running across the
			eastern end of the hallway from south to north." tell-line
			true to seen
		else here :master-bedroom = if
			"As you walk into the bedroom, you see Baxter running past you to the balcony.
			He doesn't seem to have noticed you." tell-line
			true to seen
			true :baxter-seen state!
		else here corridor-bits 1 bit-and 1 = if
			"As you enter the hallway, you see Baxter running from Dunbar's
			room across the hall to the master bedroom." tell-line
			true to seen
			true :baxter-seen state!
		then then then
	then
	:bedroom-balcony :baxter-seq-loc state!
	[ :orchard :east-lawn :north-lawn ] here position-of 0 < if
		:baxter :in-orchard move-to
		false :ladder-flag-2 state!
		:baxter :dunbar-room true establish-goal
		:i-baxter-escape 0 queue drop
		false :baxter-seq-loc state!
	then
	seen if 1 else 0 then ;

' baxter-escapes :i-baxter-escape handles

: baxter-resumes ( context -- result )
	drop
	:baxter unprioritize
	0 ;

' baxter-resumes :i-baxter-end-1 handles

\ the household gathers at Ms. Dunbar's room and disperses
: household-gathers ( context -- result )
	drop
	false to seen
	:mrs-robner :dunbar-room inside? if
		here :dunbar-room = if
			"Mrs. Robner, standing quietly by the body, starts sobbing and
			leaves the room." tell-line
		then
		:mrs-robner unprioritize
		:mrs-robner :corridor-1 move-to
		true to seen
	else :george :dunbar-room inside? if
		here :dunbar-room = if
			"George says something like ""My God"" under his breath." tell-line
		then
		:george unprioritize
	else :rourke :corridor-1 inside? if
		here :corridor-1 = if
			"Mrs. Rourke peeks in the door and looks sick. ""I'm leaving this
			house,"" she says, and pops out again." tell-line
		then
		:rourke :stair-top move-to
		:rourke :rourke-room true establish-goal
		true to seen
	then then then
	:shot-count state 1+ dup :shot-count state! 20 > if :i-shot 0 queue drop then
	seen if 1 else 0 then ;

' household-gathers :i-shot handles
